"""<p>Phones rarely break all at once; they misbehave one symptom at a time. This page is the front desk for that: find what your phone is doing, and it walks you to the guide that actually fixes it - every link is a page on this desk, written to be followed with the phone in your hand.</p>
<h2>Find your symptom</h2>
<p><b>Battery dies by mid-afternoon:</b> usually habits and background apps, not a dying battery - start with <a href="/tech/android-battery-health/">battery health and what drains it</a>, then check whether the phone itself is aging: <a href="/tech/why-phones-slow-down/">why phones slow down</a>.</p>
<p><b>The phone gets hot:</b> warmth while charging or navigating is normal; heat with performance problems is not - <a href="/tech/phone-overheating-causes-and-fixes/">overheating, causes and fixes</a> (read the swollen-battery warning; it is the one stop-everything item on this page).</p>
<p><b>Wi-Fi keeps dropping:</b> the fix order matters - phone first, then router, then the internet itself: <a href="/tech/phone-wont-connect-to-wifi/">the Wi-Fi checklist</a> and <a href="/tech/wi-fi-router-placement/">where the router should sit</a>.</p>
<p><b>Bluetooth will not pair:</b> nine times out of ten it is the pairing memory, not the hardware - <a href="/tech/bluetooth-not-pairing/">the pairing fix</a>.</p>
<p><b>Apps crash on open:</b> one app or all apps tells you which side the problem is on - <a href="/tech/app-crashes-android/">crashing apps, diagnosed</a>.</p>
<p><b>Notifications arrive late or never:</b> almost always a battery-optimisation setting, not a broken phone - <a href="/tech/android-notifications-not-arriving/">the notification fix</a>.</p>
<p><b>Mobile data not working (or vanishing fast):</b> first make it work, then make it last - <a href="/tech/mobile-data-not-working/">data not working, fixed</a>, then <a href="/tech/use-less-mobile-data/">the data diet</a>.</p>
<p><b>Storage full and apps misbehaving:</b> a full storage chip breaks apps in weird ways - clear it properly with <a href="/tech/free-up-storage-android/">the storage cleanup</a> and understand the breakage in <a href="/tech/storage-full-breaking-apps/">what a full phone breaks</a>.</p>
<p><b>Everything is just slower than it was:</b> age, storage, updates or the lot - the honest version is on <a href="/tech/why-phones-slow-down/">why phones slow down</a>.</p>
<h2>Before any of it: the two-step ritual</h2>
<p>Restart the phone (the reason it works is on <a href="/tech/why-restarting-fixes-problems/">why restarting fixes things</a>), then check storage. Those two steps clear a remarkable share of acting-up tickets, and the pages above assume you have done them. And before anything goes badly wrong for good: the backup habit - <a href="/tech/android-backup-guide/">the Android backup guide</a> - is the difference between a fix and a funeral. Ask the desk that learned it the hard way: <a href="/tech/phone-died-no-backup/">phone died, no backup</a>.</p>""",
